-- ES-5 built-in gates via cv-router /esx5gate.
--
-- Trigger path (orthogonal to the FH-2 MIDI/MCV path):
--   Tidal binding (es5gate <bit>)
--     → cv-router OSC `/esx5gate <bit> <state>` (UDP 57130)
--     → cv-router writes byte to es5_l_gates AtomicU8
--     → audio callback packs byte into high byte of the ES-5 L lane
--       (24-bit PCM ADAT, sample-rate-paced)
--     → ES-9 USB out 5/6 → ES-5 L (ADAT)
--     → ES-5 decodes high byte → 8 panel gate jacks
--
-- Bit N (0-indexed) → ES-5 panel gate (N+1) (1-indexed). Bit 0 = gate 1.
--
-- Pre-conditions:
--   1. cv-router running (default device "ES-9", listening UDP 57130):
--        cd music/expert-sleepers/cv-router && ./target/release/cv-router
--   2. ES-9 loaded with `cv-router-with-es5.es9` config so USB 5 → ES-5 L:
--        cd music/expert-sleepers/es9-config && \
--          spago run -- --live-set configs/cv-router-with-es5.es9
--   3. ES-5 module connected to ES-9 via ADAT expansion port
--
-- This is the second trigger pathway in the rig (alongside the MIDI/FH-2
-- path used by Rample, QuadDrum, Plaits). About 2× the FH-2 budget but
-- gives 8 more gate outputs without burning FH-2 MCV slots.
--
-- lat 54 = es5-trigger-baseline (single-component composition for now —
-- there's no module-specific audio engine in this path; modules
-- triggered VIA an ES-5 gate would compose es5-trigger-baseline +
-- their own audio-engine component, in a per-module setup file
-- analogous to fh2-rample / fh2-qd / fh2-plaits). See
-- docs/calibration-components.md.

bind es5g1 es5gate 0 lat 54
bind es5g2 es5gate 1 lat 54
bind es5g3 es5gate 2 lat 54
bind es5g4 es5gate 3 lat 54
bind es5g5 es5gate 4 lat 54
bind es5g6 es5gate 5 lat 54
bind es5g7 es5gate 6 lat 54
bind es5g8 es5gate 7 lat 54
